    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate focusing on high-ceiling leverage, anchored by **Isaac Paredes** (72.13) and **Corbin Carroll** (66.31). **Isaac Paredes** draws the most favorable matchup of the day against Klassen, whose 6.12 xERA creates an ideal environment for him to capitalize on a +9% platoon advantage. Meanwhile, **Corbin Carroll** remains a priority start; despite a modest -6% penalty for the lefty-on-lefty matchup against Suarez, his elite speed profile combined with a 100% stolen base opportunity against a slow-delivering pitcher makes him a core engine for our most scarce category. **Mickey Moniak** (65.81) also projects as a high-floor play, benefitting from a massive +14% park factor, though owners must monitor the 37% rain risk in his contest, as any delay could dampen his efficiency.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved the marginal utility spot, where **Josh Naylor** (44.48) narrowly edged out **Vinnie Pasquantino** (43.58). While **Vinnie Pasquantino** possesses a higher base projection, his -15% dynamic platoon penalty against Basso dropped him below our rostered threshold. **Josh Naylor** provides a safer floor despite his own struggles against southpaws, keeping him in the lineup over the bench. We are also wary of **Griffin Conine** (41.74); while his power metrics are solid, he faces a stiff test against Wheeler and a top-tier defensive catcher, forcing us to keep a close eye on his at-bats to ensure he doesn't become a drain on our AVG category. We remain without **James Wood**, who stays stashed on the IL, as we continue to lean on the current active pool to maintain our Roto standing.",
